# Styling Rules (Emotion)

- Never use Tailwind classes or raw CSS files.
- Use Emotion (`@emotion/react` or `@emotion/css`) for component styling.
- Use Emotion object notation; do not use template literal style strings.
- Do not use inline `style` attributes in JSX/TSX.

```tsx
// Bad
<main style={{ maxWidth: 420, margin: "48px auto", fontFamily: "sans-serif" }} />
```

```tsx
// Good
import { css } from "@emotion/react";

<main css={mainClass} />

const mainClass = css({
  maxWidth: 420,
  margin: "48px auto",
  fontFamily: "sans-serif",
});

```
